00:43:31.340 --> 00:43:35.080
Losing a youngster has made Obsidian even more vigilant.

00:43:52.860 --> 00:43:56.680
She retreats into the forest to nurse her two remaining cubs.

00:44:02.910 --> 00:44:07.990
No family is immune to the harsh reality of growing up in the Rockies.

00:44:09.520 --> 00:44:11.520
Life here is tenuous.

00:44:14.540 --> 00:44:18.420
And while the loss of life for one means survival for another,

00:44:19.470 --> 00:44:20.990
nothing is ever so simple.

00:44:23.330 --> 00:44:26.950
Our bison herd rushes to the place where one of their own has fallen.

00:44:29.050 --> 00:44:29.970
A female that...

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:41.390
died during labor. We gather together to mourn the loss of our loved ones. Is it so difficult to

00:44:41.390 --> 00:44:51.600
imagine that bison may do the same? Tails are raised in distress by the sight of a wolf

00:44:52.230 --> 00:44:59.370
waiting in the wings. Eventually, the herd begins to disperse.

00:45:02.910 --> 00:45:17.340
Leaving one lone three-year-old perhaps a son still grieving while his sense of smell clearly tells him she's gone

00:45:17.340 --> 00:45:29.690
He's determined to defend her a while longer. There is far more that connects us

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:47.450
separates us especially in matters of love and loss in the small clearing

00:45:47.820 --> 00:45:57.600
obsidian is still nursing her cups a shadow on the hillside above her draws

00:45:57.600 --> 00:45:59.630
her to her feet perhaps

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:19.220
passing bison. But mom is not taking any chances now. She keeps a watchful eye while her cubs play.

00:46:21.630 --> 00:46:27.760
Obsidian faces the same struggle of every parent. How much freedom is too much?

00:46:46.540 --> 00:46:50.470
As the summer sun bakes the plains, tensions are building.

00:46:53.940 --> 00:46:54.420
It's mating.

00:46:57.250 --> 00:46:59.940
And for our young calf, everything is sudden.

00:47:00.220 --> 00:47:09.330
changed for months he's been tied to his mother's side but now her attention is focused elsewhere

00:47:09.330 --> 00:47:23.620
and the large bulls he's watched all summer are suddenly too close for comfort they're agitated

00:47:23.620 --> 00:47:29.930
and chasing his mother around he tries to keep up with her but that's

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:43.310
dangerous choice this time of year bulls are competing for the right to breed and

00:47:49.030 --> 00:47:54.320
they display their fitness in the most dramatic fashion kicking clouds of dust

00:47:54.320 --> 00:47:59.900
into the as they urinate and then roll their 2,000 pound body

00:48:00.190 --> 00:48:01.430
against the bare earth.

00:48:03.800 --> 00:48:05.880
This bull is sending a message.

00:48:07.040 --> 00:48:08.860
It's a chemical billboard.

00:48:11.050 --> 00:48:15.020
It tells the other bulls he is at the peak of his game.

00:48:30.600 --> 00:48:35.580
One of the large bulls is sticking close to the calf's mother, tending her.

00:48:44.120 --> 00:48:46.020
But he's treading a difficult path.

00:48:50.090 --> 00:48:53.710
He's surrounded, and the competition is stiff.

00:49:01.020 --> 00:49:05.680
If he wants to keep her to himself, he's going to have to prove that he can.

00:49:20.450 --> 00:49:22.570
It's a deadly, serious game.

00:49:32.170 --> 00:49:38.610
The success of future generations depends upon the outcome of these gladditorial battles.

00:49:43.630 --> 00:49:49.450
And as the two bulls exhaust themselves, someone seizes an opening.

00:50:18.520 --> 00:50:22.460
Amidst the chaos, the calves seek comfort in each other.

00:50:28.380 --> 00:50:29.740
And as with every competition,

00:50:30.480 --> 00:50:43.900
there is a victor these are the calves last days of childhood and in just a few years they'll

00:50:43.900 --> 00:50:56.560
compete for real if they hope to be so fortunate they must endure all that the rockies have in

00:50:56.560 --> 00:50:58.790
store for them in the months ahead

00:51:06.200 --> 00:51:12.660
As colors shift into autumn, Obsidian's calm demeanor has returned.

00:51:17.780 --> 00:51:19.980
She calls for her two remaining cubs.

00:51:22.460 --> 00:51:29.170
Now, at the end of their season, her cubs are chubby and confident as they follow after mom.

00:51:30.890 --> 00:51:38.060
Soon, Obsidian and her cubs will retreat to the warmth and safety of their winter den.

00:51:39.620 --> 00:51:48.610
While some take refuge underground, others must prepare to head south to outrun winter's icy grip.

00:51:51.110 --> 00:51:55.870
But for many others, they will have to endure winter's fury head-on.

00:51:59.310 --> 00:51:59.970
There will be battle...

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:10.440
to fight and alliances to forge. Some must rely on the strength of their tribe

00:52:10.440 --> 00:52:22.080
while others must go it alone. For all these brave souls, the experience of

00:52:22.080 --> 00:52:26.840
growing up in the Rockies has only just begun.

